---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import toolRegistry from '../data/tool-registry.json';
import { FaqSection } from '../components/ui/FaqSection';
import { generateFAQSchema, generateBreadcrumbSchema, generateWebApplicationSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const seo = {
  title: 'Complete Wedding Planning Checklists & Interactive Tools (2026)',
  description: 'The ultimate month-by-month wedding planning checklist and 14 free interactive tools: Guest List Manager, Budget Calculator, Timeline Generator, Milestone Tracker & Countdown.',
  canonical: 'https://www.weddingplanningchecklists.org/'
};

const siteUrl = 'https://www.weddingplanningchecklists.org';
const breadcrumbItems = [
  { name: 'Home', item: siteUrl }
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is a wedding planning checklist?', a: 'A wedding planning checklist is a step-by-step guide that helps couples organize every stage of their wedding, from setting a budget and booking a venue to sending invitations and preparing for the wedding day. It ensures no important task is overlooked.' },
  { q: 'When should you start planning your wedding?', a: 'Most wedding experts recommend starting 12 to 18 months before your wedding date. This gives you enough time to book popular venues, hire vendors, manage your budget, and avoid last-minute stress.' },
  { q: 'What should be booked first when planning a wedding?', a: 'Your wedding venue should be booked first because it determines your wedding date. Once your venue is confirmed, you can book photographers, caterers, florists, entertainment, and other vendors.' },
  { q: 'How much does a typical wedding cost?', a: 'Wedding costs vary depending on location, guest count, and style. Your budget should include venue, catering, photography, decorations, attire, entertainment, transportation, and an emergency fund for unexpected expenses.' },
  { q: 'Can I plan a wedding without hiring a wedding planner?', a: 'Yes. Many couples successfully plan their weddings using detailed checklists, budget trackers, timelines, and planning tools. A day-of coordinator can still be helpful for managing the event itself.' },
  { q: 'What should a wedding budget include?', a: 'A complete wedding budget should include venue rental, food, beverages, photography, videography, decorations, flowers, invitations, wedding attire, entertainment, transportation, favors, taxes, gratuities, and a contingency budget.' },
  { q: 'How do I create a wedding guest list?', a: 'Start with immediate family and close friends, then add extended family, colleagues, and acquaintances based on your venue capacity and overall budget. Prioritize guests who are most important to you as a couple.' },
  { q: 'What vendors should I hire for my wedding?', a: 'Most weddings require a venue, photographer, videographer, caterer, florist, DJ or live band, officiant, hair and makeup artist, transportation service, baker, and rental company.' },
  { q: 'How far in advance should wedding invitations be sent?', a: 'Save-the-date cards are usually sent 6 to 8 months before the wedding. Formal invitations are typically mailed 6 to 8 weeks before the ceremony, allowing guests enough time to RSVP.' },
  { q: 'What is included in a printable wedding checklist?', a: 'A printable wedding checklist typically includes monthly planning tasks, vendor booking timelines, guest list management, budgeting, ceremony planning, reception planning, honeymoon preparation, and wedding day essentials.' },
  { q: 'How do I stay organized while planning a wedding?', a: 'Use a digital or printable wedding planner to track tasks, deadlines, budgets, vendor contracts, guest RSVPs, and payment schedules. Reviewing your checklist weekly helps keep everything on schedule.' },
  { q: 'What is the most stressful part of wedding planning?', a: 'Couples often find managing the budget, finalizing the guest list, coordinating multiple vendors, and meeting deadlines to be the most challenging aspects of wedding planning.' },
  { q: 'What should be in a bridal emergency kit?', a: 'A bridal emergency kit should include safety pins, fashion tape, stain remover, tissues, pain relievers, bandages, deodorant, lipstick, hairpins, sewing kit, snacks, water, phone charger, and mints.' },
  { q: 'How can I save money when planning a wedding?', a: 'Set a realistic budget, prioritize essential expenses, reduce your guest count, compare vendor quotes, consider off-season dates, and choose DIY decorations where appropriate.' },
  { q: 'What should be done one month before the wedding?', a: 'Confirm vendor bookings, finalize seating arrangements, obtain your marriage license, complete dress fittings, prepare vendor payments, and create a detailed wedding day timeline.' },
  { q: 'How do I choose the perfect wedding venue?', a: 'Consider your guest count, budget, wedding style, location, accessibility, available services, parking, weather backup options, and vendor flexibility before making your decision.' },
  { q: 'Is a wedding website necessary?', a: 'While not required, a wedding website makes it easy to share event details, RSVP information, travel recommendations, gift registries, schedules, and updates with guests.' },
  { q: 'How long does it take to plan a wedding?', a: 'Most weddings take between 12 and 18 months to plan, although smaller weddings or elopements can often be organized within 3 to 6 months with careful planning.' },
  { q: 'What happens if I have only six months to plan my wedding?', a: 'Focus first on booking your venue, photographer, caterer, and officiant. Simplify decorations, reduce DIY projects, and use a structured checklist to prioritize essential tasks.' },
  { q: 'Where can I find a free wedding planning checklist?', a: 'You can download a free wedding planning checklist from WeddingPlanningChecklists.org. It includes monthly timelines, budget planning, vendor checklists, guest list organization, and wedding day preparation resources.' }
];

const combinedSchema = `[${[
  generateWebApplicationSchema({ name: 'Wedding Planning Checklists', description: seo.description, url: seo.canonical }),
  generateFAQSchema(faqs),
  generateBreadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbItems)
].filter(Boolean).join(',')}]`;
---

<BaseLayout title={seo.title} description={seo.description} canonical={seo.canonical} schemaScript={combinedSchema}>
  <Header />

  <main class="space-y-16">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="relative py-20 lg:py-28 overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-b from-[#FCECF0]/50 via-white to-transparent">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 text-center space-y-6">
        <span class="inline-block bg-[#FCECF0] text-[#B76E79] px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider shadow-sm">
          The Ultimate Planning Experience
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-extrabold text-[#1A1A1A] leading-tight tracking-tight">
          Complete Wedding Planning Checklists for <span class="text-[#B76E79]">Your Big Day</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Welcome! We've built a dedicated suite of tools to help you manage your guest list, track budgets, and book vendors without the stress.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4 pt-4">
          <a href="/tools/wedding-planning-dashboard" class="bg-[#B76E79] hover:bg-[#a25d66] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-full text-sm font-bold shadow-lg transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-0.5">
            Start Planning Now
          </a>
          <a href="/tools/guest-list-manager" class="bg-white hover:bg-slate-50 text-[#1A1A1A] border border-slate-200 px-8 py-4 rounded-full text-sm font-bold transition-all shadow-sm">
            Guest List Manager
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Proof Stats -->
        <div class="pt-12 grid grid-cols-3 max-w-2xl mx-auto gap-4 border-t border-[#F3E8EA] mt-10">
          <div>
            <p className="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-[#1A1A1A]">120k+</p>
            <p className="text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">Tasks Completed</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p className="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-[#B76E79]">50k+</p>
            <p className="text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">Guests Managed</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p className="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-[#D4AF37]">$20M+</p>
            <p className="text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">Budgets Saved</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Key Features Overview -->
    <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-6">
      <div class="text-center space-y-3 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-[#1A1A1A]">Everything You Need for Your Dream Wedding</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm max-w-xl mx-auto">Orchestrate your wedding with priority-sorted task managers, budget calculators, and RSVP trackers.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-2xl bg-[#FCECF0] text-[#B76E79] flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg">✓</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-[#1A1A1A]">Smart Checklist</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">Manage every detail with our priority-sorted task manager organized by timeline.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-2xl bg-[#FCECF0] text-[#B76E79] flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg">👥</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-[#1A1A1A]">Guest List</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">Keep track of RSVPs, dietary needs, meal choices, seating, and plus-ones easily.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-2xl bg-[#FCECF0] text-[#B76E79] flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg">💰</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-[#1A1A1A]">Budget Tracker</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">Never overspend with real-time allocation across venue, catering, photo & buffer.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm space-y-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-2xl bg-[#FCECF0] text-[#B76E79] flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg">📅</div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-[#1A1A1A]">Timeline Planner</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">Visual milestone maps and time-blocked daily schedules for your big day.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 14 Interactive Planning Tools Grid -->
    <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10">
      <div class="text-center space-y-3 mb-12">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#B76E79] uppercase tracking-wider">Interactive Suite</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-[#1A1A1A]">14 Free Interactive Wedding Planning Tools</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-xl mx-auto text-sm">
          All tools sync automatically with your wedding date and save your progress safely in your browser.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        {toolRegistry.tools.map(tool => (
          <a
            href={tool.href}
            class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-[#B76E79]/40 transition-all group flex flex-col justify-between"
          >
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <span class="inline-block text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#B76E79] bg-[#FCECF0] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">
                {tool.category}
              </span>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-[#1A1A1A] group-hover:text-[#B76E79] transition-colors">{tool.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">{tool.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pt-4 flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-bold text-[#B76E79]">
              <span>Use Tool</span>
              <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Comprehensive Educational Article Guide -->
    <section class="max-w-[700px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 prose prose-slate">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl border border-[#F3E8EA] p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm space-y-8">
        
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-[#1A1A1A] leading-tight">
            Plan Your Dream Wedding Without Missing a Single Detail
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
            Planning a wedding is one of the most exciting journeys of your life — and one of the most overwhelming. With hundreds of tasks, dozens of vendors, and thousands of decisions to make, even the most organized couples can feel lost. That is exactly why having a well-structured wedding planning checklist is the single most important tool you can use from the moment you get engaged.
          </p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
            Our complete wedding planning checklists guide covers everything — from setting your budget 12 months out to packing your bridal emergency kit the night before your big day. Whether you are planning a grand ballroom celebration, a destination wedding, a cozy backyard ceremony, or a traditional Pakistani or Indian wedding, this checklist keeps every task, timeline, and vendor organized in one place.
          </p>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-[#F3E8EA]" />

        <!-- What Is Section -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">
            What Is a Wedding Planning Checklist and Why Do You Need One?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            A wedding planning checklist is a structured, step-by-step to-do list that organizes every task involved in planning your wedding — sorted by priority, timeline, and category.
          </p>
          <p class="text-slate-700 font-semibold text-sm">Without one, couples often:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600">
            <li>Forget to book vendors until it is too late</li>
            <li>Overspend because there is no budget tracking</li>
            <li>Miss deadlines for invitations, RSVPs, or final payments</li>
            <li>Feel stressed and overwhelmed in the final weeks</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            With a proper wedding planner checklist, you always know exactly what needs to be done next, what has been completed, and what requires your attention today.
          </p>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-[#F3E8EA]" />

        <!-- Month-by-Month Section -->
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">
            The Ultimate Month-by-Month Wedding Planning Checklist
          </h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            This is the most comprehensive month-by-month wedding checklist available — organized from engagement day to honeymoon morning.
          </p>

          <!-- 12 Months -->
          <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-base text-[#B76E79]">✅ 12 Months Before the Wedding</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">This is the foundation stage. The decisions you make now save you thousands of dollars and enormous stress later.</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs text-slate-700 pt-2">
              <div>
                <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1A1A] mb-1">Budget & Vision</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1">
                  <li>Set your total wedding budget</li>
                  <li>Decide how many guests to invite</li>
                  <li>Define your wedding style and theme</li>
                  <li>Discuss must-haves vs. nice-to-haves</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="font-bold text-[#1A1A1A] mb-1">Venue & Key Vendors</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1">
                  <li>Book ceremony and reception venue</li>
                  <li>Lock in official wedding date</li>
                  <li>Book photographer & videographer</li>
                  <li>Hire wedding planner/coordinator</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- 9 Months -->
          <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-base text-[#B76E79]">✅ 9 Months Before the Wedding</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">With your venue secured, build out the rest of your vendor team and finalize your aesthetic.</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-xs text-slate-700">
              <li>Begin shopping for wedding dress (Allow 4–6 months for production)</li>
              <li>Choose bridesmaids' attire and groomsmen suits</li>
              <li>Hire florist, caterer, and cake designer</li>
              <li>Design save-the-dates and build wedding website</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- 6 Months -->
          <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-base text-[#B76E79]">✅ 6 Months Before the Wedding</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Shift into high gear: invitations, travel, rentals, and hair/makeup trials.</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-xs text-slate-700">
              <li>Order wedding invitations and mail save-the-dates</li>
              <li>Book honeymoon travel, hotel room blocks, and rehearsal dinner venue</li>
              <li>Schedule hair and makeup trials</li>
              <li>Book wedding rentals (chairs, linens, lighting)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- 3 Months & 1 Month -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-5 space-y-2">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-[#B76E79]">✅ 3 Months Before</h4>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1 text-xs text-slate-700">
                <li>Mail wedding invitations</li>
                <li>Track RSVPs & finalize headcount</li>
                <li>Create seating chart & table cards</li>
                <li>Finalize ceremony vows & music</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-5 space-y-2">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-[#B76E79]">✅ 1 Month Before</h4>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1 text-xs text-slate-700">
                <li>Obtain marriage license</li>
                <li>Final dress fitting & break in shoes</li>
                <li>Assemble bridal emergency kit</li>
                <li>Prepare vendor tip envelopes</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Wedding Week -->
          <div class="bg-[#FCECF0]/40 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-[#B76E79]/20 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-base text-[#B76E79]">✅ Wedding Week & Day-Of Checklist</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Final venue walkthrough, rehearsal dinner, device charging, bridal emergency kit packing, and enjoying every single moment!</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-[#F3E8EA]" />

        <!-- Bridal Emergency Kit Table -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">
            The Essential Bridal Emergency Kit Checklist
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Pack these essentials the night before your wedding day:</p>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
              <thead>
                <tr class="bg-[#FCECF0] text-[#B76E79]">
                  <th class="p-3 font-bold rounded-l-xl">Category</th>
                  <th class="p-3 font-bold rounded-r-xl">Items</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">Beauty</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">Lipstick/gloss, bobby pins, hairspray, blotting papers, safety pins</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">Health</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">Pain reliever, antacids, allergy medication, bandages</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">Wardrobe</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">Stain remover pen, fashion tape, needle and thread, extra earring backs</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">Practical</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">Phone charger, cash, vendor contact list, marriage license reminder</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">Comfort</td><td class="p-3 text-slate-600">Breath mints, snacks, water bottle, comfortable backup shoes</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-[#F3E8EA]" />

        <!-- Budget Breakdown Table -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">
            Wedding Budget Checklist: Know Where Every Cent Goes
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Recommended budget allocation by category:</p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-5 gap-3 text-center">
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100"><span class="block text-base font-bold text-[#B76E79]">40–45%</span><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-semibold">Venue & Catering</span></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100"><span class="block text-base font-bold text-[#B76E79]">10–12%</span><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-semibold">Photo & Video</span></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100"><span class="block text-base font-bold text-[#B76E79]">8–10%</span><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-semibold">Flowers & Décor</span></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100"><span class="block text-base font-bold text-[#B76E79]">5–8%</span><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-semibold">Attire & Rings</span></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100"><span class="block text-base font-bold text-[#D4AF37]">5–10%</span><span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-semibold">Emergency Buffer</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-[#F3E8EA]" />

        <!-- Cultural & Special Wedding Types -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">
            Wedding Checklists for Every Type of Wedding
          </h3>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-2xl space-y-1">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-[#1A1A1A]">Pakistani & Muslim Weddings</h4>
              <p class="text-slate-600">Spans multiple events: Mehndi, Baraat, Nikkah, and Walima. Separate logistics and outfit tracking per event.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-2xl space-y-1">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-[#1A1A1A]">Destination Weddings</h4>
              <p class="text-slate-600">Passport renewals, travel insurance, guest logistics, and booking 18 months in advance.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-2xl space-y-1">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-[#1A1A1A]">Backyard & DIY Weddings</h4>
              <p class="text-slate-600">Restroom rentals, generator power access, tenting, permits, and dedicated DIY project timelines.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-2xl space-y-1">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-[#1A1A1A]">Intimate / Small Weddings</h4>
              <p class="text-slate-600">Fewer guests, enabling focus on elevated personalized details, fine dining, and photography.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Latest Articles Grid -->
    <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 bg-slate-50/50 border-t border-slate-100">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]">Latest from Our Blog</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Expert tips and aesthetic inspiration for your big day.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/blog" class="text-xs font-bold text-[#B76E79] hover:underline">View All Articles →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <a href="/blog/14-month-wedding-planning-timeline" class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all group">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#B76E79] uppercase">Planning</span>
